ative implementation of the function.\n            Focus on different approaches (e.g., list comprehensions, loops).\n            Include all necessary imports and handle edge cases.\n            Return ONLY the executable Python code.\n            """,\n            context=extraction\n        )\n        \n        alternative_2 = await self.generate(\n            instruction="""\n            Generate another alternative implementation of the function.\n            Focus on efficiency and clarity.\n            Include all necessary imports and handle edge cases.\n            Return ONLY the executable Python code.\n            """,\n            context=extraction\n        )\n        \n        # Use Ensemble to select the best implementation\n        final_code = await self.ensemble(\n            instruction="""\n            Evaluate the following implementations and select the best one:\n            1. Compare their correctness, efficiency, and Pythonic style.\n            2. Choose the implementation that best meets the problem requirements.\n            3. Return ONLY the selected Python code.\n            """,\n            contexts=[revised_code, alternative_1, alternative_2]\n        )\n        \n        # Step 5: Final validation and refinement\n        final_refinement = await self.revise(\n            instruction="""\n            Validate the final implementation and make any final refinements:\n            1. Ensure it passes all test cases.\n            2. Optimize for performance if needed.\n            3. Add documentation if necessary.\n            Return ONLY the final, refined Python code.\n            """,\n            context=final_code\n        )\n        \n        return final_refinement\n```', '<think>\n</think>\n\n</think>\n\n```python\n# --- DO NOT IMPORT HERE ---\nclass Workflow:\n    def __init__(self, config, problem) -> None:\n        # --- DO NOT MODIFY THIS SECTION ---\n        self.config = config\n        self.problem_text = problem\n    